## `entry_hash` — DC-3, not an invented construction

`entry_hash` is **DC-3**, declared at `framework.manifest.json`
`metadata.reproducible.digest_constructions.ledger_entry_hash` by `AIEF-AMD-008` §AMD-17
(approval `approvals/APR-002`), disposing `ecr/ECR-Q-002`. Seven covered fields in the
declared order — `seq`, `timestamp`, `session_id`, `actor`, `action`, `artifacts`,
`prev_hash` — each serialised as one `<field-name> <SP> <value> <LF>` record, concatenated
with no header or trailer. `entry_hash` is excluded from its own preimage. `prev_hash` is
the literal token `null` at genesis, and is a covered field, so it feeds the successor
digest and makes the chain tamper-evident rather than merely sequential.

**The digest domain is that canonical preimage, never these on-disk octets** — the manifest
states that file layout, key order, comments and whitespace do not affect the value. This
file therefore follows the grammar of its sibling `../HEAD`; no serialisation was invented
here, and none was needed.

The implementation used was validated against **both** worked examples the manifest
publishes (`entry_1` → `cb8e7972…8259e0`, `entry_2` → `66e51617…f8195b`, and the
eleven-octet empty-`artifacts` record) **before** this entry was written, because the
transition it performs cannot be undone.

